<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Adolf II, Duke of Saxe-Weissenfels</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1685">1685</a>–<a href="/years/1746">1746</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Adolf II was the last duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxe-weissenfels">Saxe-Weissenfels</a>, ruling from 1736 to 1746. A field marshal in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> army, he commanded Saxon forces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a> and was defeated by the Prussians at Hohenfriedberg in 1745. On his death the duchy reverted to the Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-adolf-ii-duke-of-saxe-weissenfels.jpg" alt="Johann Adolf II, Duke of Saxe-Weissenfels" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antoine Pesne · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antoine_Pesne_(1683-1757)_-_John_Adolphus_II,_Duke_of_Saxe-Weissenfels_(1685-1746)_-_RCIN_405656_-_Royal_Collection.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
